comment6.params=img\ text\ font\ centerX\ centerY
comment6.target=void\ drawCenteredStringXOR(greenfoot.GreenfootImage,\ java.lang.String,\ greenfoot.Font,\ int,\ int)
comment6.text=\n\ Draws\ text\ centered\ on\ (centerX,\ centerY),\ XOR-ing\ it\ with\ whatever\ is\ already\ in\ the\ image.\n\ With\ white\ as\ the\ draw\ color\ and\ black\ as\ the\ XOR\ color,\ every\ pixel\ the\ text\ covers\ is\n\ inverted\ (dst\ ^\ 0xFFFFFF),\ so\ it\ stays\ readable\ on\ any\ background.\n
comment7.params=img\ x\ y\ width\ height\ thickness\ color
comment7.target=void\ drawBorder(greenfoot.GreenfootImage,\ int,\ int,\ int,\ int,\ int,\ java.awt.Color)
comment7.text=\n\ Draws\ a\ rectangular\ border\ of\ exactly\ `thickness`\ pixels.\ The\ border\ lies\ entirely\ INSIDE\ the\n\ given\ box,\ so\ the\ box's\ outer\ size\ is\ exactly\ width\ x\ height\ (nothing\ spills\ out\ or\ gets\ clipped).\n
comment8.params=img\ x\ y\ width\ height\ thickness\ color
comment8.target=void\ drawBorderXOR(greenfoot.GreenfootImage,\ int,\ int,\ int,\ int,\ int,\ java.awt.Color)
comment9.params=img\ centerX\ centerY\ width\ height\ thickness\ color\ inverted
comment9.target=void\ drawThickRectAt(greenfoot.GreenfootImage,\ int,\ int,\ int,\ int,\ int,\ java.awt.Color,\ boolean)
comment9.text=Draws\ a\ border\ of\ the\ given\ size,\ centered\ on\ (centerX,\ centerY)\ of\ the\ image.
